CloudBurrow patch 30 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1370). Applies after patch 0029.

The gap: BigQuery refuses an UPDATE, DELETE, MERGE or TRUNCATE TABLE that
would change a row written by tabledata.insertAll (the Storage Write API
(REST)) "within the last 30 minutes"; "all other rows in the table remain
modifiable" (https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/data-manipulation-language).
That needs each streamed row's time, on any table, partitioned or not.

The patch makes a table column named _PARTITION_STREAMED a pseudo-column,
as patch 0028 makes _PARTITIONTIME one: SELECT * leaves it out, an INSERT
may give it and a query names it. bigquery-emulator patch 0018 gives every
table made by tables.insert the column, TIMESTAMP, and CloudBurrow's front
sets it to the time of a streamed row. BigQuery reserves the column-name
prefix _PARTITION, so no column of a table can be named so.
streamed_at_column_test.go fails without the patch and passes with it.

